      "summaries": {
        "en": "Res-downloader is a Go-based tool that simplifies downloading media from popular Chinese platforms like Douyin and WeChat, addressing the challenge of accessing content from these often-restricted services. It works by reverse-engineering platform APIs to bypass download limitations, teaching users about web scraping techniques for resource extraction. You can use it via command-line to batch download videos or music, or integrate its core logic into custom applications for automated media collection.",
        "zh": "Res-downloader 是一个基于 Go 语言开发的工具，专门用于从抖音、微信视频号、快手、小红书等中国主流平台下载视频和音乐资源，解决了这些平台通常限制直接下载的难题。它通过逆向工程分析平台API，绕过下载限制，展示了如何利用网络爬虫技术提取受保护资源。用户可以通过命令行快速批量下载内容，或将其核心模块集成到自定义应用中，实现自动化媒体收集，适合内容存档、研究分析或离线观看等场景。",
        "es": "Res-downloader is a Go-based tool that simplifies downloading media from popular Chinese platforms like Douyin and WeChat, addressing the challenge of accessing content from these often-restricted services. It works by reverse-engineering platform APIs to bypass download limitations, teaching users about web scraping techniques for resource extraction. You can use it via command-line to batch download videos or music, or integrate its core logic into custom applications for automated media collection.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "res-downloader stands out for douyin, kuaishou, and res-downloader in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Res-downloader is a Go-based tool that simplifies downloading media from popular Chinese platforms like Douyin and WeChat, addressing the challenge of accessing content from these often-restricted services. It works by reverse-engineering platform APIs to bypass download limitations, teaching users about web scraping techniques for resource extraction. You can use it via command-line to batch download videos or music, or integrate its core logic into custom applications for automated media collection.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/putyy/res-downloader for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
