      "summaries": {
        "en": "MLX-Audio is an open-source library that enables efficient speech processing on Apple Silicon devices, solving the challenge of running complex audio AI models locally without cloud dependency. Built on Apple's MLX framework, it leverages hardware-optimized computation to deliver fast text-to-speech, speech-to-text, and speech-to-speech conversion with minimal latency. Developers can integrate it into macOS applications for voice interfaces, create accessible tools, or experiment with multimodal AI pipelines using its transformer-based architecture.",
        "zh": "MLX-Audio 是一个基于苹果 MLX 框架的开源音频处理库，专为 Apple Silicon 设备优化，让开发者能在本地高效运行语音 AI 模型而无需依赖云端。它通过硬件加速计算，实现了低延迟的文本转语音、语音转文本及语音转换功能，其核心在于利用 MLX 的并行计算能力提升推理速度。你可以将其集成到 macOS 应用中构建智能语音交互功能，开发无障碍工具，或基于其 Transformer 架构尝试多模态 AI 实验，探索端侧语音处理的更多可能性。",
        "es": "MLX-Audio is an open-source library that enables efficient speech processing on Apple Silicon devices, solving the challenge of running complex audio AI models locally without cloud dependency. Built on Apple's MLX framework, it leverages hardware-optimized computation to deliver fast text-to-speech, speech-to-text, and speech-to-speech conversion with minimal latency. Developers can integrate it into macOS applications for voice interfaces, create accessible tools, or experiment with multimodal AI pipelines using its transformer-based architecture.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "mlx-audio stands out for apple-silicon, audio-processing, and mlx in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "MLX-Audio is an open-source library that enables efficient speech processing on Apple Silicon devices, solving the challenge of running complex audio AI models locally without cloud dependency. Built on Apple's MLX framework, it leverages hardware-optimized computation to deliver fast text-to-speech, speech-to-text, and speech-to-speech conversion with minimal latency. Developers can integrate it into macOS applications for voice interfaces, create accessible tools, or experiment with multimodal AI pipelines using its transformer-based architecture.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/Blaizzy/mlx-audio for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
